{
  "_comment": [
    "Source registry for the morning brief.",
    "",
    "'lean' is a coarse, editorially-contested label. It is NOT used to filter anything out.",
    "It is used for exactly two things:",
    "  1. Diversity scoring - a story covered across several leans ranks above a story",
    "     covered by many outlets that all share one lean.",
    "  2. Transparency - the app shows you the spread so you can judge it yourself.",
    "",
    "'wire' marks agency/wire-service style desks whose house style is closest to",
    "plain declarative reporting. Wire headlines win ties when picking the headline",
    "to show, because they are least likely to be framed for engagement.",
    "",
    "Add or remove sources freely. The pipeline degrades gracefully: any feed that",
    "fails to fetch or parse is skipped and reported in the build log.",
    "",
    "Every URL here responded with parseable items on a live probe (GitHub Actions,",
    "2026-08-23). Reuters was dropped: apnews.com, reuters.com and reutersagency.com",
    "all return 401/404 to feed readers now. UPI, the Washington Times and CBC were",
    "unreachable. Re-run the Probe feeds workflow when the digest looks thin.",
    "",
    "One feed per outlet, always. Two feeds from the same newsroom would each count",
    "as a distinct source and inflate the consensus score for that outlet's stories.",
    "",
    "Feeds carry an 'outlet' separate from their id. Several newsrooms contribute",
    "more than one feed (BBC world + BBC technology). Consensus counts distinct",
    "OUTLETS, so those count once - otherwise a newsroom with four desks would",
    "look like four independent confirmations of the same story.",
    "",
    "'topic' marks a topic-scoped feed and is the strongest classification signal.",
    "Topic feeds were probed live on 2026-09-01; all 28 responded."
  ],
